{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.94,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["SW6", "R34", "R35"],
      "pins": ["SW6.1", "SW6.2", "SW6.3", "SW6.4", "R34.1", "R35.1"],
      "nets": ["/CAN0_P", "/CAN1_P", "/CAN0_N", "/CAN1_N"],
      "observed": "The two poles of SW6 connect across the two CAN interfaces: one pole joins /CAN0_P to /CAN1_P, and the other joins the ends of R34 and R35, whose opposite ends are on /CAN0_N and /CAN1_N. Closing both poles therefore bridges the two CAN buses; closing only the N-side pole couples their negative lines through the two 120-ohm resistors.",
      "expected": "CAN0 and CAN1 should remain separate buses, as specified. If SW6 is intended to select termination, each 120-ohm resistor should terminate its own bus across that bus's P and N lines, rather than coupling the two buses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_P : ... SW6.4(passive) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN1_P : ... SW6.3(passive) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_N : ... R34.1(1,passive) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN1_N : ... R35.1(1,passive) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R34-Pad2) : R34.2(2,passive) SW6.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R35-Pad2) : R35.2(2,passive) SW6.2(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "In switch positions that close both poles, the CAN transceiver outputs and differential bus signals can be tied together, defeating bus separation and potentially causing contention or unreliable communication. The N-side coupling can also load the buses even without the P-side pole closed.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    }
  ],
  "summary": "SW6 can electrically couple the two CAN interfaces, contrary to the specified separate CAN0 and CAN1 buses. The netlist shows each switch pole connecting corresponding lines or termination-resistor ends across the interfaces."
}

